WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.943
[MUSIC]

00:00:02.943 --> 00:00:07.372
Welcome and
congratulations to the GSB class of 2020.

00:00:07.372 --> 00:00:10.148
Welcome also to families and
friends, we're so

00:00:10.148 --> 00:00:13.750
happy to have people join us from
everywhere around the world.

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:19.590
This is not the graduation weekend
anyone anticipated although honestly,

00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:22.620
I don't miss wearing my academic
regalia in the hot sun.

00:00:23.770 --> 00:00:29.320
But perhaps it's appropriate, the class
of 2020 has been a pioneering class,

00:00:29.320 --> 00:00:31.900
a class that will not be
forgotten at the GSB.

00:00:32.930 --> 00:00:33.930
And so once again,

00:00:33.930 --> 00:00:38.780
we break new ground, the GSB's first
virtual celebration of graduates.

00:00:39.940 --> 00:00:44.170
When you arrived I asked you,
what did you want to learn?

00:00:44.170 --> 00:00:46.360
What kind of community
did you want to build?

00:00:46.360 --> 00:00:48.070
What kind of leader did
you want to become?

00:00:49.290 --> 00:00:52.870
I hope you have at least partial
answers to those questions.

00:00:52.870 --> 00:00:56.020
As I told you, the GSB would be awesome,
I hope it was.

00:00:57.110 --> 00:01:00.150
I told you there would be adversity and
opportunity.

00:01:00.150 --> 00:01:05.200
None of us foresaw the scale,
a global pandemic, and

00:01:05.200 --> 00:01:08.800
a national and
global uprising against racial injustice.

00:01:10.230 --> 00:01:14.830
The last few months have revealed our
vulnerability, the fragility of human life

00:01:14.830 --> 00:01:17.730
and the many ways in which we
can inflict harm on one another.

00:01:18.770 --> 00:01:20.970
They've revealed our inner dependence.

00:01:20.970 --> 00:01:25.430
The extent to which we rely on the work
and support and love of others.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:28.870
They've highlighted challenges
that existed before the pandemic.

00:01:28.870 --> 00:01:32.630
Society to polarized inequities too wide.

00:01:32.630 --> 00:01:36.910
Reservoirs of trust that we need
today were depleted, in government,

00:01:36.910 --> 00:01:40.240
in organizations, in experts,
in our fellow citizens.

00:01:41.680 --> 00:01:46.870
Which brings me to you,
you are graduating at a momentous time.

00:01:46.870 --> 00:01:50.420
I'd like to ask the question,
what does the world need from you?

00:01:51.830 --> 00:01:54.210
You are going forth with many advantages.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:59.440
You have Stanford degrees, the skills to
succeed in any endeavor, a strong network.

00:01:59.440 --> 00:02:02.360
You've shown your leadership
skills at the GSB.

00:02:02.360 --> 00:02:06.624
You're positioned for professional
success, and I hope you achieve it.

00:02:06.624 --> 00:02:11.051
I also want to say, don't let that
be enough, I encourage you now and

00:02:11.051 --> 00:02:16.480
as you go through your careers to think
hard about your metrics for success.

00:02:16.480 --> 00:02:19.280
There'll be visible and
tangible measures, the money you make,

00:02:19.280 --> 00:02:21.760
your investing track record,
the stock price of your company.

00:02:23.140 --> 00:02:26.560
I hope you'll measure success
by the way you treat others and

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.750
the opportunities you create for
them, whether that's individually or

00:02:30.750 --> 00:02:34.180
by helping to narrow inequities and
bring people together.

00:02:35.870 --> 00:02:40.170
Remember that business is both
a powerful economic force and

00:02:40.170 --> 00:02:45.285
a powerful societal force that gives
business leaders great influence,

00:02:45.285 --> 00:02:49.170
be leaders of business and
leaders for society.

00:02:51.642 --> 00:02:54.290
I want to finish by quoting
to you some words from former

00:02:54.290 --> 00:02:56.900
President Franklin Delano Roosevelt.

00:02:56.900 --> 00:02:59.844
In 1932 in the depths of
the Great Depression,

00:02:59.844 --> 00:03:04.376
which was another momentous time he
spoke to graduates in Atlanta, Georgia.

00:03:04.376 --> 00:03:07.920
And this is what he said to them,
still resonates today.

00:03:09.010 --> 00:03:10.560
We need enthusiasm,

00:03:10.560 --> 00:03:15.640
imagination, and the ability to face
facts, even unpleasant ones bravely.

00:03:15.640 --> 00:03:19.400
We need to correct by drastic means,
if necessary the faults in our economic

00:03:19.400 --> 00:03:23.190
system from which we now suffer,
we need the courage of the young.

00:03:24.260 --> 00:03:28.240
Yours is not the task of making
your way in the world, but

00:03:28.240 --> 00:03:31.910
the task of remaking the world,
which you will find before you.

00:03:33.630 --> 00:03:37.780
You too are graduating at a time when
it's important to face facts bravely,

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.620
to correct flaws in our system,
to rebuild.

00:03:40.620 --> 00:03:45.960
I know each of you has the capacity not
just to make your way but to rise high,

00:03:45.960 --> 00:03:51.410
don't leave it at that, help rebuild
in the way that raises others.

00:03:51.410 --> 00:03:55.620
Set yourself the task of remaking
a better world around you.

00:03:55.620 --> 00:03:57.474
That's what will set you apart.

00:03:59.365 --> 00:04:04.613
Next, we're going to show a video of your
GSB experience which I hope captures

00:04:04.613 --> 00:04:09.538
how transformative and maybe how
awesome your time at the GSB has been.

00:04:13.669 --> 00:04:18.516
[MUSIC]

00:04:18.516 --> 00:04:21.794
&gt;&gt; This is not a normal year, we've
been looking at each other on screen and

00:04:21.794 --> 00:04:24.070
occasionally from a distance
of six feet or more.

00:04:25.070 --> 00:04:29.470
As you know, Stanford is a special place,
the beauty of the campus,

00:04:29.470 --> 00:04:33.070
the ability to learn from brilliant
faculty, the culture of collaboration and

00:04:33.070 --> 00:04:35.070
optimism, and most of all the people.

00:04:36.100 --> 00:04:40.680
During your time at the GSB you've gone
from being a set of individuals to being

00:04:40.680 --> 00:04:45.710
a class that's held together by bond that
even social distancing cannot diminish.

00:04:45.710 --> 00:04:48.900
The pandemic has shown how much
the world needs leaders for

00:04:48.900 --> 00:04:54.230
society, who make decisions based
on data and reason, who act boldly,

00:04:54.230 --> 00:05:00.130
who demonstrate compassion and
inspire others, you are those leaders.

00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:04.147
We are counting on you to bring
your ideas, your experience, and

00:05:04.147 --> 00:05:07.371
your passion to whatever you do and
wherever you go.

00:05:07.371 --> 00:05:10.896
[MUSIC]

00:05:10.896 --> 00:05:16.465
&gt;&gt; Congratulations to
the Stanford Graduate School of

00:05:16.465 --> 00:05:22.420
Business Class of 2020,
I am so proud of all of you.

00:05:22.420 --> 00:05:25.510
What you have accomplished Is remarkable.

00:05:25.510 --> 00:05:31.080
You have put yourselves on a journey
towards making a big impact in the world.

00:05:31.080 --> 00:05:38.010
Simply put, you are the absolute
best of our future leaders.

00:05:39.050 --> 00:05:44.900
Now, I know this is not exactly
the graduation you were all expecting.

00:05:44.900 --> 00:05:51.584
At the same time, today's adversity
makes your class a truly historic one.

00:05:51.584 --> 00:05:57.080
And for now, congratulations on
your incredible achievement and

00:05:57.080 --> 00:05:59.936
welcome to the GSB alumni family.

00:05:59.936 --> 00:06:09.936
[MUSIC]

00:06:13.943 --> 00:06:16.790
&gt;&gt; This is the end of
your time at the GSB.

00:06:16.790 --> 00:06:21.350
But as Orlando just said, it's
the beginning of your time as GSB alumni,

00:06:21.350 --> 00:06:24.230
the next stage of your relationship
with the school and your classmates.

00:06:25.740 --> 00:06:29.670
I look forward to the time, hopefully soon
when I can welcome you back to campus

00:06:29.670 --> 00:06:34.070
with Orlando, and your families and
friends for traditional commencement.

00:06:34.070 --> 00:06:38.648
In the meantime, I'm so
proud of what you've accomplished and

00:06:38.648 --> 00:06:40.441
what your future holds.

00:06:40.441 --> 00:06:50.441
[MUSIC]

